{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"trustful-combative-grackle","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The gap\n\nNothing enforces that the extras installed by `test.yml`'s sweep lanes track the extras installed\nby `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` (the gating Verified lane). The two can diverge\nsilently, and when they do, a test can pass on the gating lane and fail on every sweep lane — or\nthe reverse, which is worse, because then the gate is the one that is blind.\n\n`tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` exists to catch workflow divergence. **It was modified by\nthe very commit that introduced this divergence (`c57057f41`) and did not catch it.** A parity\ncheck that does not cover the dimension that actually drifted provides confidence without\ncoverage.\n\n## The concrete instance that motivated this\n\n`c57057f41` (\"Enable the grounding-terraform extra\") added `--extra grounding-terraform` to\n`_build-and-test.yml` and `_optionality.yml` but NOT to `test.yml`. Result, on main at\nee2c54f881d6 (run 33905162633):\n\n- `build-and-test / pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)` — installs the extra — **PASSED**\n- `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` — does not — **FAILED**\n- `sweep (py3.14)` — does not — **FAILED**, byte-identical assertion\n\nThe proximate defect (a test missing an `importorskip` guard) is tracked separately as\n`87b8-1339-383f-43f6` and is being fixed. THIS ticket is about the missing invariant that let the\ntwo lanes drift apart unnoticed in the first place.\n\n## Why this is worth its own ticket rather than folding into the fix\n\nGuarding the one test makes main green. It does not stop the next extra from being added to one\nworkflow and not the other. The lanes have DIFFERENT and deliberate install sets — the sweep\nlanes are intentionally lean, which is their whole purpose — so the invariant is NOT \"the install\nlines must be identical\". It is something more careful: a divergence must be DELIBERATE and\nVISIBLE rather than accidental.\n\nThat is a design question, which is why the acceptance criteria below do not prescribe the\nmechanism.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — A check fails when an extra is added to the gating lane's install but not to the\n      sweep lanes' (or vice versa) WITHOUT an explicit, in-tree declaration that the divergence is\n      intended. Prove it by introducing such a divergence and observing the check fail.\n- [ ] AC2 — A DELIBERATE divergence remains expressible and passes. The sweep lanes are\n      intentionally leaner than the gating lane; the check must not force them to converge, or it\n      will simply be disabled the first time it is inconvenient.\n- [ ] AC3 — The check names WHICH extra diverged and in WHICH direction, so the failure is\n      actionable without reading both workflow files side by side.\n- [ ] AC4 — Re-running the check against `c57057f41`'s tree (the commit that introduced the real\n      divergence) FAILS. This is the anti-vacuity criterion: a check that would not have caught\n      the known historical instance has not been shown to work.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot changing which extras any lane installs — the current lean/gating split is deliberate and\ncorrect. Not fixing the missing `importorskip` guard (that is `87b8-1339-383f-43f6`). Not\nwidening the sweep lanes.","id":"9c64-7582-ffad-4fea","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"No invariant ties test.yml sweep-lane extras to the gating lane's extras, so they drift silently; test_ci_workflow_parity was edited by the very commit that diverged them and did not catch it"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788546913939063001,"uuid":"5d5f5c02-f1d8-47e7-9306-d49462bc5c93"}